# Testing

## Purpose

Cover behavior (repos, BLoCs) with the existing test stack — no new frameworks.

## When Applied

Adding or editing tests under `test/` or `integration_test/`.

## Requirements

- Mirror the `lib/` path in `test/` (e.g. `test/features/booking/...`).
- Use `flutter_test` + `bloc_test`; mock the repository, not Supabase globals.
- Prioritize: repository mapping/error handling, BLoC/Cubit state transitions, cache-first behavior.
- Keep tests deterministic — no live network/Supabase calls.
- See [`docs/testing-guide.md`](../../../docs/testing-guide.md).

## Examples

```dart
blocTest<BookingBloc, BookingState>(
  'emits [loading, loaded] on start',
  build: () => BookingBloc(mockRepo),
  act: (b) => b.add(BookingStarted()),
  expect: () => [BookingLoading(), isA<BookingLoaded>()],
);
```

## Anti-patterns

- Introducing a new mocking/test framework outside the project's set.
- Tests that hit real Supabase or depend on wall-clock timing.

## Common Mistakes

- Asserting UI instead of the BLoC state contract.
- Forgetting to test the `PostgrestException` → user-safe mapping.
